.TH PIS 1 "7 November 2026" "pis 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pis \- Slackware 15.0 post-installation configuration assistant
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pis
.RI [ option ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B PIS
is a dialog-based collection of Bash scripts for selected Slackware 15.0
post-installation tasks. It configures locale, keyboard, login, users, wheel
administration, X sessions, ELILO kernels and selected package managers.
.PP
Before replacing a configuration file, PIS creates a private backup under
.IR /var/log/PIS/backups .
PIS can display and restore these backups.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show command help.
.TP
.BR -v , " --version"
Show the installed version.
.TP
.BR -c , " --check"
Display the system and compatibility check.
.TP
.BR -o , " --output " FILE
Export settings recorded by PIS to a versioned profile. Passwords are not
exported.
.TP
.BR -f , " --file " FILE
Validate, preview and apply a PIS profile.
.TP
.B --restore
Select and restore an automatic PIS backup.
.SH PROFILES
PIS 0.3 profiles use
.B PIS_PROFILE_VERSION=1
and store portable values such as the full slackpkg mirror URL. Unknown
settings, incompatible repositories and invalid values are rejected before
changes are made. A password is requested interactively when a missing user
must be created.
.PP
PIS 0.2 profiles are rejected because they may contain plaintext passwords.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/log/PIS
Private state recorded by PIS.
.TP
.I /var/log/PIS/backups
Automatic backups and their index.
.TP
.I /boot/efi/EFI/Slackware/elilo.conf
ELILO configuration, when the kernel module is used.
.SH NOTES
PIS uses existing Slackware configuration files and does not replace the
distribution's network and service configuration utilities.
